CYBRA MODULE 15 — TRUE_100 AGGREGATOR CONTROLLER
PATCH_ID=CYBRA-M15-PATCH-0001

1. TRUE_100 means 100% of all required conditions are confirmed.
2. 0–99% MUST NOT be TRUE_100.
3. Missing required evidence MUST prevent TRUE_100.
4. Invalid required evidence MUST prevent TRUE_100.
5. Conflicting evidence MUST prevent TRUE_100.
6. A single failed required module MUST prevent TRUE_100.
7. A single pending required module MUST prevent TRUE_100.
8. Required signatures MUST be independently confirmed.
9. Required delivery evidence MUST be independently confirmed.
10. Required buyer receipt MUST be independently confirmed.
11. Required Backend A confirmation MUST be present.
12. Required Backend B confirmation MUST be present.
13. Backend A/B state hashes MUST match where required.
14. Required watchdog condition MUST be PASS.
15. Required rules/state hashes MUST match.
16. TRUE_100 MUST NOT be created by percentage rounding.
17. 99.99% MUST NOT be treated as 100%.
18. A missing condition MUST remain missing.
19. A conflict MUST remain a conflict until independently resolved.
20. Hypothesis MUST NOT be converted into evidence.
21. Inference MUST NOT be converted into evidence.
22. TEST evidence MUST NOT automatically become LIVE evidence.
23. TRUE_100 does not itself authorize escrow release.
24. TRUE_100 does not itself authorize LIVE.
25. TRUE_100 does not itself send a blockchain transaction.
26. Final release requires explicit final authorization.
27. The aggregator MUST NOT manufacture evidence.
28. The aggregator MUST NOT manufacture signatures.
29. The aggregator MUST NOT manufacture backend confirmations.
30. The aggregator MUST NOT manufacture delivery or receipt evidence.
31. Every correction MUST create a new PATCH_ID.
32. Frozen snapshots MUST NOT be silently modified.
33. GLOBAL_TRUE_100 belongs to the complete CYBRA state machine.
34. Module 15 may report a TRUE_100 candidate only when every required gate is independently satisfied.
35. A TRUE_100 candidate MUST remain FALSE if any required gate is unresolved.
